From 62c12d7406d34fef034c8e59cb3bf079aa2c5c81 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gordan <gordan.radic@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 02:30:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] NBR: ffmpeg stops depending on the video libraries it is told
 not to use

The build had been failing on libvpl for two runs, and failing SILENTLY:
ninja stops, ffmpeg and mpv never configure, no mpv-dev artifact is produced
-- and the run still reports success. The only trace is that ffmpeg-prefix's
stamp folder holds a download log and nothing else, where every package that
really built holds configure and build logs too.

libvpl is Intel's hardware VIDEO codec runtime. Nothing in this cut asks for
it: ffmpeg's configure here is --disable-everything plus exactly ten external
libraries, all audio (libmodplug, libopenmpt, libopus, libsoxr, libspeex,
libvorbis, libbs2b, openssl, libxml2, libmysofa). It was in DEPENDS only
because upstream's DEPENDS is written for a video player's ffmpeg.

So fifteen names go, and every one is both (a) absent from this ffmpeg's
enable list and (b) absent from mpv's own DEPENDS, which is what decides
whether it still has to be built at all -- the build runs `ninja mpv`, so a
package no target depends on is never touched:

    libvpx libwebp libzimg x264 x265 libvpl libjxl libzvbi
    libaribcaption aom svtav1 dav1d uavs3d davs2 libva

Everything else stays, including the ones this ffmpeg does not enable but mpv
still needs (libass, libplacebo, vapoursynth, rubberband, openal-soft) and
the cheap ones it auto-detects (bzip2).

The failure mode if this is wrong is a loud one: ffmpeg's configure says
"ERROR: libX not found" and the build stops. That is the right way round.

The Bell's branch did the same thing on 2026-09-07 and its note says why:
"the first build spent 90 minutes on video libraries and died on libvpl".
---
 packages/ffmpeg.cmake | 15 ---------------
 1 file changed, 15 deletions(-)

diff --git a/packages/ffmpeg.cmake b/packages/ffmpeg.cmake
index 811e317..cc756f9 100644
--- a/packages/ffmpeg.cmake
+++ b/packages/ffmpeg.cmake
@@ -14,32 +14,17 @@ ExternalProject_Add(ffmpeg
         libpng
         libsoxr
         libbs2b
-        libvpx
-        libwebp
-        libzimg
         libmysofa
         fontconfig
         harfbuzz
         opus
         speex
         vorbis
-        x264
-        ${ffmpeg_x265}
         libxml2
-        libvpl
         libopenmpt
-        libjxl
         libplacebo
-        libzvbi
-        libaribcaption
-        aom
-        svtav1
-        dav1d
         vapoursynth
-        ${ffmpeg_uavs3d}
-        ${ffmpeg_davs2}
         rubberband
-        libva
         openal-soft
     GIT_REPOSITORY https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg.git
     SOURCE_DIR ${SOURCE_LOCATION}
-- 
2.55.0.windows.2

